.\" sysstat.pcpconf.5 - Manual page for the sysstat PCP local metric config file
.TH SYSSTAT.PCPCONF 5 "JUNE 2026" "sysstat-@PACKAGE_VERSION@" "Linux User's Manual" -*- nroff -*-
.SH NAME
sysstat.pcpconf \- sysstat PCP local metric collection configuration file
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B sysstat.pcpconf
file configures which additional metrics
.BR sadc (8)
records from a local PMDA context when writing PCP archives
(via
.B \-O pcp
or
.BR "\-O sa+pcp" ).
It is read once at
.B sadc
startup; changes take effect on the next restart.
.PP
The default location is
.IR @SYSCONFIG_DIR@/sysstat.pcpconf .
The
.B PCP_CONF
environment variable overrides this path.
.SH "FILE FORMAT"
The file uses a simple INI-style format.  Lines beginning with
.B #
are comments.  Blank lines are ignored.
Section headers are enclosed in square brackets.
.SS "[settings]"
Key\-value pairs controlling collection behaviour.
.TP
.BI "volume_size = " bytes
Maximum PCP data volume size in bytes before automatic rotation.
Set to 0 to disable in-session rotation.  Default: 0.
.SS "[pmdas]"
One PMDA name per line.  Each entry is passed to
.BR pmSpecLocalPMDA (3)
before opening the local context.  The
.B proc
PMDA is always loaded automatically; entries in this section add
optional extras such as
.BR linux .
.SS "[metrics]"
One metric name per line.  Both leaf metric names
(e.g.\&
.IR proc.psinfo.pid )
and namespace node names
(e.g.\&
.IR proc.psinfo )
are accepted; namespace nodes are expanded to all leaf metrics
beneath them via
.BR pmTraversePMNS (3).
.PP
Metrics whose PMID is already registered by
.BR sadc 's
built-in write path are silently skipped to avoid double-writes.
Unknown metric names are skipped with a warning on stderr.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
[settings]
interval = 15

[pmdas]
# linux

[metrics]
proc.nprocs
proc.psinfo.pid
proc.psinfo.cmd
proc.psinfo.utime
proc.psinfo.stime
proc.memory.vmrss
proc.io.read_bytes
proc.io.write_bytes
proc.id.uid_nm
proc.fd.count
proc.schedstat.run_delay
.fi
.SH "ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES"
.TP
.B PCP_CONF
Overrides the configuration file path.  Useful for testing or
site-specific deployments.
.SH FILES
.I @SYSCONFIG_DIR@/sysstat.pcpconf
.RS
Default configuration file location.
.RE
.I /etc/pcp/pmlogconf/tools/pidstat
.br
.I /var/lib/pcp/config/pmlogconf/tools/atop-proc
.RS
PCP-provided metric lists that can be used as a reference for
populating the
.B [metrics]
section.
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR sadc (8),
.BR sa1 (8),
.BR sa2 (8),
.BR pmSpecLocalPMDA (3),
.BR pmTraversePMNS (3),
.BR sysstat (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Sebastien Godard (sysstat <at> orange.fr)
